<!--div id="onScreenHelp"> Can't find what you're looking for? <a  href="/static/faq.html" target=faq_window > Click here.</a> </div-->
<div id="searchDiv">
Keyword Search <div id="searchHints" onclick="setVisibility('hintsDiv', 'block');">Hints</div>
<div id="hintsDiv" >
<h3>Keyword Search Hints:<div id="closeSearchHints" onclick="setVisibility('hintsDiv', 'none');">Close(X)</div></h3>
<p>
The keyword search feature allows you to search using any word.  For any keyword that you enter, all matching items will be returned (i.e. a search for "Corn" will yield results for Corn, Sweet Corn, and Popcorn).  Once you have initiated a search by keyword, you can then proceed to limit by any other available Selections.
</p>
<p>
If you enter two or more keywords, the results will include entries for all entered keywords.  Example:  a search for "apple orange" will yield results for any items containing the word orange OR the word apple.
</p>
<p>
The keyword search is not case sensitive.
</p>
<p>
Search is currently only enabled for commodities.
</p>
</div>
<form id="search_form" name="search_form" method="Get" action="https://quickstats.nass.usda.gov/" onsubmit ="javascript:displayRowCounts();submitSearch();" >
   <div id="search_text_spinner" class="spinner" style="width:200;display:none;" ><img src='/static/images/indicator.gif'/></div>
<!--
-->
   <!--input id="search_text" ="text" dojoType="dijit.form.TextBox" style="height:24px;" name="long_desc__LIKE" value="" -->
   <input id="search_text" ="text" dojoType="dijit.form.TextBox" style="height:24px;" name="long_desc__LIKE" value="" >
   <button  id='search' dojoType="dijit.form.Button" type="submit" value="Search">Search</button>
<!--
-->
   <button id="resetSearch" dojoType="dijit.form.Button" name="RESET"  onclick="javascript:goHome(); return false;" >Clear</button>
   &nbsp;&nbsp;
   <!--
   -->
</form>
</div>
