   </div>
   <div id="NavHistoryDiv" style="border:0px gray dashed " > 
   </div>

   <br>
   <br>
   <div class="selectTable" style="border:0px gray dashed">
        
            	
                <div class="selectHeader">	
                    <div class="subheading" >
                        <!-- 
                        Select Commodity (select one or more) <div id="Commodityhelp" style="float:right" ><img onclick="toggleHelp('Commodity_help');" height="20px" width="20px" src="/static/images/help-icon.png"></div>
                        -->
                        Select Commodity <div id="Commodityhelp" style="float:; display:inline;cursor:pointer;margin:3px;font-size:11px" >(one or more) &nbsp;<img onclick="toggleHelp('Commodity_help');" " src="/static/images/icon_help_bubble.gif" alt="Online Help"></div>
                        <div id="Commodity_help" class="contextHelp">
                          <div id="closeSearchHints" onclick="toggleHelp('Commodity_help');">Close(X)</div>
                            <br>
                              <p>
	Quick Stats lets you create queries based on the simple filtering rules of <em>What, Where</em>, and <em>When</em>.</p>
<p>
	<strong>Select Commodity</strong> is the <em>What</em>. Click on a value from any visible item list to start your query.  The remaining visible unselected item lists will filter and refresh based on your choices. If the updated fields in the Select Commodity area are satisfactory, you will not have to make more selections in this area unless you want to fine tune your search.</p>

<p>
	You may begin filtering in Select Commodity, Select Location or Select Time areas. For example, if you want the most recent corn data, you would start by filtering on Select Time.</p>
<p>
	If you would like to select more than one item in any of the data fields, hold the Ctrl key on your keyboard and click on any other items of the same field that you would like to use.&nbsp; You may also hold the Shift key and select an upper and lower value of a data field to select the entire range.&nbsp;</p>
 
                          </div>
                   </div>
                   <br clear="all">
                </div>
                
