                              <p>
	<span _fck_bookmark="1" style="display: none">&nbsp;</span><span _fck_bookmark="1" style="display: none"> </span>Quick Stats lets you create queries based on the simple filtering rules of <em>What, Where, </em>and<em> When</em>.</p>
<p>
	<strong>Select Location</strong> is the <em>Where</em>. Click on a value from any visible item list to start your query.  The remaining visible unselected item lists will filter and refresh based on your choices. If the updated fields in the Select Location area are satisfactory, you will not have to make more selections in this area unless you want to fine tune your search.</p>

<p>
	You may begin filtering in the Select Location, Select Commodity or Select Time areas. For example, if you want the most recent corn data, you would start by filtering on Select Time.</p>
<p>
	If you would like to select more than one item in any of the data fields, hold the <strong>Ctrl</strong> key on your keyboard and click on any other items of the same field that you would like to use.&nbsp; You may also hold the <strong>Shift</strong> key and select an upper and lower value of a data field to select the entire range.&nbsp;<span _fck_bookmark="1" style="display: none"> </span></p>

 
